 of everything in the gym  from resistance training to tone muscle  to core strength building workouts she  also engaged in activities as diverse as  kickboxing rock climbing and of course  tons of cardio the end result of this  variety of work is overall fitness and  the body that's generally muscular with  no one muscle group exaggerated after  all ray isn't a muscle-bound warrior  she's just a generally fit person and  for the movies sake she needs to look  like it personal trainers the main  trainer really worked  early on was Jack graves a former rugby  player which may have something to do  with the grueling cardio work that went  into our routines but while graves did  the work for Ridley's general fitness  she also worked with more specialized  trainers for activities specific to Star  Wars like swinging swords around in  close quarters combat which saw her  training with a stuntman and  choreographer who also helped design the  fight sequences for the last Jedi and  Ridley told vogue those lightsabers are  heavier than they look weighing in at  about 10 pounds so she really needed the  conditioning they're really heavy three  four five kilos and the weights very  unevenly distributed a positive outlook  in one of Britney's old Instagram posts  she made a point about how what we see  on Instagram really corresponds to  reality and that's a fitness post while  inspiring hardly told the whole story I  have a trainer urging me on in workouts  and I don't include all the times I say  I can't do it what she did include  though was positivity and excitement and  enthusiasm for the work even when she  wasn't at her best as one characteristic  post read for anyone that's gonna try  and correct my form I know it isn't the  best I've just started doing sprint  training so progressing all the time  this sort of positive outlook matters as  just knowing that just because you're  not your best right now it doesn't mean  you won't get better thanks for watching  click the